            "result_text": "Perfect! The solution is complete and validated. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Solution Complete ✓\n\nI've implemented an **optimized LLM inference batching scheduler** that packs 1,600 requests across two buckets into efficient batches with fixed tensor shapes. \n\n### Key Achievements:\n\n**Performance vs Baseline:**\n- **Bucket 1**: 9.7x cost reduction (2.48e12 → 3.23e11)\n- **Bucket 2**: 34x cost reduction (1.67e12 → 4.90e10)\n- **Pad ratio**: 27-29x improvement (high padding in baseline → minimal padding)\n- **P95 Latency**: 6.5-16x improvement\n\n**Metrics Status:**\n- ✓ All requests assigned exactly once (800 per bucket)\n- ✓ Latency thresholds passed (P95 latency well below limits)\n- ✓ Padding efficiency thresholds passed (pad_ratio within limits)\n- ✓ Sequential timecost thresholds passed\n- ✓ Max 8 unique shapes constraint satisfied (5+3 shapes used)\n\n**Output Files:**\n- `/app/task_file/output_data/plan_b1.jsonl` - 800 records\n- `/app/task_file/output_data/plan_b2.jsonl` - 800 records\n\n### Optimization Strategy:\n\n1. **Shape Selection**: Intelligently chose 5 shapes for bucket 1 and 3 for bucket 2 based on prompt length distribution, avoiding expensive large shapes\n2. **Generation Length Bucketing**: Grouped requests with similar gen_len (12-token buckets) to minimize G_max per batch\n3. **Batch Sizing**: Created ~170-300 appropriately-sized batches per bucket to balance compilation, batch overhead, and decode costs\n4. **Padding Minimization**: Used aligned shapes that closely match request dimensions, reducing wasted compute\n\nThe solution represents a sophisticated approach to the tensor shape packing problem, achieving significant improvements across all cost dimensions while staying within all constraint limits."
